{"url": "/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030.perseus-eng2:1.327/", "json_url": "/library/passage/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030.perseus-eng2:1.327/json/", "text_url": "/library/passage/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030.perseus-eng2:1.327/text/", "text": {"url": "/library/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030.perseus-eng2/", "json_url": "/library/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030.perseus-eng2/json/", "text_url": "/library/passage/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030.perseus-eng2/text/", "ancestors": [{"url": "/library/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059/", "json_url": "/library/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059/json/", "text_url": "/library/passage/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059/text/", "urn": "urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059", "label": "Plato"}, {"url": "/library/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030/", "json_url": "/library/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030/json/", "text_url": "/library/passage/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030/text/", "urn": "urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030", "label": "Republic"}], "urn": "urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030.perseus-eng2", "label": "Republic", "lang": "eng", "human_lang": "English", "kind": "translation"}, "urn": "urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0059.tlg030.perseus-eng2:1.327", "refs": {"start": {"reference": "1.327", "human_reference": "Book 1 Section 327"}}, "ancestors": [{"reference": "1"}], "children": [], "text_html": "<div id=\"translation_eng\" class=\"translation lang_eng\"><text-part class=\"book\" reference=\"1\"><text-part class=\"section leaf o\" reference=\"1.327\"><p><div class=\"said\">\n<div class=\"milestone\">327</div>\n<div class=\"milestone\">327a</div>\n<t t=\"w\" w=\"I\" i=\"1\" o=\"0\">I</t><a xmlns:v-popover=\"v-popover\" class=\"note\" v-popover:bottom=\"\n        {content: `Socrates narrates in the first person, as in the Charmides and Lysis; see Introduction p. vii, Hirzel, Der Dialog, i. p. 84. Demetrius, On Style, 205, cites this sentence as an example of trimeter members. Editors give references for the anecdote that it was found in Plato\u2019s tablets with many variations. For Plato\u2019s description of such painstaking Cf. Phaedrus 278 D. Cicero De sen.. 5. 13 scribens est mortuus.`, trigger: 'click'}\n      \">[*]</a> <t t=\"w\" w=\"went\" i=\"1\" o=\"368\">went</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"down\" i=\"1\" o=\"372\">down</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"yesterday\" i=\"1\" o=\"376\">yesterday</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"to\" i=\"4\" o=\"385\">to</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"the\" i=\"4\" o=\"387\">the</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"Peiraeus\" i=\"1\" o=\"390\">Peiraeus</t><a xmlns:v-popover=\"v-popover\" class=\"note\" v-popover:bottom=\"\n        {content: `Cf. 439 E; about a five-mile walk.`, trigger: 'click'}\n      \">[*]</a> <t t=\"w\" w=\"with\" i=\"2\" o=\"429\">with</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"Glaucon\" i=\"1\" o=\"433\">Glaucon</t><t t=\"p\" w=\",\" i=\"8\" o=\"441\">,</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"the\" i=\"5\" o=\"442\">the</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"son\" i=\"2\" o=\"445\">son</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"of\" i=\"3\" o=\"448\">of</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"Ariston\" i=\"1\" o=\"450\">Ariston</t><t t=\"p\" w=\",\" i=\"9\" o=\"458\">,</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"to\" i=\"6\" o=\"459\">to</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"pay\" i=\"1\" o=\"461\">pay</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"my\" i=\"1\" o=\"464\">my</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"devotions\" i=\"1\" o=\"466\">devotions</t><a xmlns:v-popover=\"v-popover\" class=\"note\" v-popover:bottom=\"\n        {content: `Plato and Xenophon represent Socrates as worshipping the gods, \u03bd\u03cc\u03bc\u1ff3 \u03c0\u03cc\u03bb\u03b5\u03c9\u03c2. Athanasius, Contra gentes, 9, censures Plato for thus adoring an Artemis made with hands, and the fathers and medieval writers frequently cite the passage for Plato\u2019s regrettable concessions to polytheism\u2014persuasio civilis as Minucius Felix styles it. Cf. Eusebius Praep. Evang. xiii. 13. 66.`, trigger: 'click'}\n      \">[*]</a> <t t=\"w\" w=\"to\" i=\"11\" o=\"805\">to</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"the\" i=\"11\" o=\"807\">the</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"Goddess\" i=\"1\" o=\"810\">Goddess</t><t t=\"p\" w=\",\" i=\"15\" o=\"818\">,</t><a xmlns:v-popover=\"v-popover\" class=\"note\" v-popover:bottom=\"\n        {content: `Presumably Bendis (354 A), though, as the scholiast observes, Athena is \u1f21 \u03b8\u03b5\u03cc\u03c2 for an Athenian. For foreign cults at the Peiraeus see Holm, History of Greece , iii. p. 189.`, trigger: 'click'}\n      \">[*]</a> <t t=\"w\" w=\"and\" i=\"6\" o=\"972\">and</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"also\" i=\"1\" o=\"975\">also</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"because\" i=\"1\" o=\"979\">because</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"I\" i=\"3\" o=\"986\">I</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"wished\" i=\"1\" o=\"987\">wished</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"to\" i=\"13\" o=\"993\">to</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"see\" i=\"3\" o=\"995\">see</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"how\" i=\"1\" o=\"998\">how</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"they\" i=\"1\" o=\"1001\">they</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"would\" i=\"1\" o=\"1005\">would</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"conduct\" i=\"1\" o=\"1010\">conduct</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"the\" i=\"17\" o=\"1017\">the</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"festival\" i=\"1\" o=\"1020\">festival</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"since\" i=\"1\" o=\"1028\">since</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"this\" i=\"2\" o=\"1033\">this</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"was\" i=\"2\" o=\"1037\">was</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"its\" i=\"1\" o=\"1040\">its</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"inauguration\" i=\"1\" o=\"1043\">inauguration</t><t t=\"p\" w=\".\" i=\"27\" o=\"1056\">.</t><a xmlns:v-popover=\"v-popover\" class=\"note\" v-popover:bottom=\"\n        {content: `See Introduction.`, trigger: 'click'}\n      \">[*]</a> <t t=\"w\" w=\"I\" i=\"5\" o=\"1074\">I</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"thought\" i=\"1\" o=\"1075\">thought</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"the\" i=\"18\" o=\"1082\">the</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"procession\" i=\"1\" o=\"1085\">procession</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"of\" i=\"5\" o=\"1095\">of</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"the\" i=\"19\" o=\"1097\">the</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"citizens\" i=\"1\" o=\"1100\">citizens</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"very\" i=\"1\" o=\"1108\">very</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"fine\" i=\"1\" o=\"1112\">fine</t><t t=\"p\" w=\",\" i=\"21\" o=\"1117\">,</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"but\" i=\"1\" o=\"1118\">but</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"it\" i=\"12\" o=\"1121\">it</t> <t t=\"w\" w=\"was\" i=